/*
 * zakapp.mjs
 *
 * The app side of everything settled on 6-7 September: the messages, the
 * COD conversation, the customer's replies, and the merchant's own phone.
 *
 * 1. Dates. One delivery date instead of a range - seven working days
 *    from the order, four from the hand-over to the courier, Sundays
 *    skipped, always in India's clock (the server runs on UTC, so the
 *    delivered stamp used to be five and a half hours out).
 *
 * 2. Templates. The customer's name is dropped from every message after
 *    the first contact, and the variables are renumbered to match. The
 *    sender now knows BOTH numberings and uses whichever a template really
 *    has - so the templates can be edited in Meta one a day, in any order,
 *    and no message is ever garbled or refused while that goes on.
 *    Refund no longer names the payment method ("razorpay" is not a bank).
 *
 * 3. Cash on Delivery. Silence after the reminder now means yes: the order
 *    is confirmed, tagged cod-auto-confirmed, and packed - nothing is ever
 *    cancelled for silence. Each of the three messages has its own switch,
 *    the reminder's hours and the wait after it are settings, and the
 *    Cancel button works: before dispatch the order is cancelled after the
 *    grace period, after dispatch the customer is told to decline at the
 *    door.
 *
 * 4. Replies. Every customer message gets an answer inside the 24-hour
 *    window: Change address and Change phone number ask for the new one,
 *    file it on the Shopify order (note + tag) and thank them; Help asks
 *    what went wrong; a typed question about the parcel gets its live
 *    status; a greeting or an unreadable message gets a short apology and
 *    a tap-menu (Track / Change address / Change phone number / Cancel /
 *    Something else). STOP is honoured and acknowledged once.
 *
 * 5. Your own WhatsApp. Whatever a customer writes in their own words -
 *    a new address, a complaint, a message the app could not read - is
 *    forwarded to the number set on the settings page, as the owner_alert
 *    template, with what the app replied. Confirm and Cancel taps are
 *    handled and not forwarded.
 *
 * 6. Pay online. Rs 30 on one item (PREPAID30), Rs 20 an item on more -
 *    the same deal the store's popup shows - in the Pay Now offer, its
 *    link, and the fallback order form. The link stops working 48 hours
 *    after the offer and says so.
 *
 * 7. Prepaid orders get one message, "payment received", not "order
 *    placed" as well. The COD twin cancelled by an online payment sends no
 *    cancellation message. A failed delivery says why in plain words.
 *
 * 8. Settings page: the keys show only their last four characters, with
 *    Change and Remove; the one-time code goes by SMS first once an SMS
 *    provider exists; new switches for all of the above.
 *
 * Every file it touches is copied to ..\zak-bak first, and a file that is
 * not the version this script was built against is left alone and named.
 * Run it from the repo root.
 */

